diag-rssi: invalid option -- '-'

Usage: diag-rssi [-flag 1 <parameter>] [-flag 2 <parameter>] ...

	-v <vendor_id>		The vendor ID of the modem device.
	-p <product_id>		The product ID of the modem device.
	-i <mdm_interface>	The interface to use on the modem device.
	-a <endpoint_in>	The IN endpoint address of the device.
	-b <endpoint_out>	The OUT endpoint address of the device.

	-S 			Use this flag to only display info from packets with SCH > 1.
	-T 			Use this flag to only display RSSI totals.
	-t 			Use this flag to print packet timestamps.
	-f 			Use this flag to print frame/subframe numbers.

	-l <0|1>		Logging msg output: 0 for standard out, 1 for the syslog.
	-d <0|1|2>		Set debug level from 0 (lowest, least output) to 2 (highest).
	-s 			Include this flag to save settings to config file.
	-h 			Use this flag to print this usage info.

	Any missing parameters will use the values from the config file.
	If a config file cannot be found or there are certain settings missing from the
	config file, default values will be used for those settings.

